  "schemaVersion": 9,
  "note": "Closed routing map. Route only a validated typed operator outcome and failure.owningDomain. A chain inserts goal-derived prerequisite work into the same user host session; child workers never create sibling user sessions.",
  "kinds": {
    "operator": "Invoke the named operator next.",
    "resume": "Invoke the same operator again with the required delta from its resume token.",
    "chain": "Plan prerequisite work whose goal is the named operator primary output inside the current host session. The blocked branch waits and re-enters with the validated delta. Keep the same goal authority and shared worker limit; do not ask a person for an already authorized repair.",
    "user": "Stop. A person owns this and must decide or publish before the mission continues.",
    "external": "Stop. The blocker is outside the runtime and no operator can clear it.",
    "helper": "Run the named helper on its declared profile inside the current host session context. Its support run record remains under @worktrees/helpers/<id>/runs/<runId>/; it is not a product operator branch and cannot write source or perform publication. User entry only; stop codes do not route to helpers.",
    "bank": "Take scripts/bank.mjs#next from the approved product bank. Run one entry at a time using the same host binding, record mission.bankRef, mark running:<sessionId>, and mark done:<sessionId> only after its goal is proved. Dependencies and a blocked entry pause the bank. Approval remains bound to the queue content hash; a changed goal needs renewed authority."
  },
